  "term": "PChE",
  "definition": "PChE stands for plasmatic cholinesterase, a blood-based biomarker used to monitor pesticide intoxication. In this context, it refers to a laboratory measure that may be checked when evaluating pesticide exposure, although normal PChE levels may still occur despite long-term exposure effects.",
